{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/812403-options-to-expand-kith-based-abilities","id":812403,"title":"Options to expand Kith-based abilities?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-19T23:03:11-08:00","id":812403,"title":"Options to expand Kith-based abilities?","content":"Just wondering, but will there be options in the form of specific powers or merits that expand upon the abilities of a particular kith? I noticed in the original Changeling the Lost that despite there being a theme of you turning more other as your gained Wyrd, there was not a whole lot of changes actually associated with it. Maybe I missed something when I went to dig into it, but high Wyrd supposedly brings about more changes in changelings, but it's not really reflected too well. It's at maybe 7+ Wyrd that changes become noticeable, and even then it's just a larger number associated with the existing ability (Eg. +1 becomes a +3). Part of me thinks it'd be neat if there were Wyrd-related and Kith-related merits tied to expressing the changeling's ongoing transformation into the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T23:21:02-08:00","id":812406,"title":"","content":"I could see merits for Seemings, but I'd imagine there are far too many Kiths for it to be feasible to expand Kiths in such a way. <br /> Though, because of the thematic changes with Seeming and Kith, that result actually makes sense to me. I mean, why would the Wyrd increase the manifestation of your durance when it could enhance the manifestation of the escape that ties you to the wyrd strongly enough that it warps and alters your kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-20-2016, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T23:24:55-08:00","id":812409,"title":"","content":"In Equinox Road, the rules for Wyrd Evolution were presented for Wyrd 7+ changelings, as well as a number of powerful merits available only to high Wyrd characters. In Winter Masques, an optional rule allowed changelings to take on new Kiths at Wyrd 4 and 7, I think. These are all still considered canon until otherwise contradicted in 2E texts.<br /> <br /> Wyrd stuff will be explored, and possibly some with Kiths, though given the plans around Kiths and the fact that they number about a hundred already, we're hesitant to make Kith-specific merits like they existed in the previous supplements.<br /> <br /> But yeah, this is stuff we're looking at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T06:32:32-08:00","id":812552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/812403-options-to-expand-kith-based-abilities?p=812409#post812409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Equinox Road, the rules for Wyrd Evolution were presented for Wyrd 7+ changelings, as well as a number of powerful merits available only to high Wyrd characters. In Winter Masques, an optional rule allowed changelings to take on new Kiths at Wyrd 4 and 7, I think. These are all still considered canon until otherwise contradicted in 2E texts.<br /> <br /> Wyrd stuff will be explored, and possibly some with Kiths, though given the plans around Kiths and the fact that they number about a hundred already, we're hesitant to make Kith-specific merits like they existed in the previous supplements.<br /> <br /> But yeah, this is stuff we're looking at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe merits with some possibly overlap? I don't know, but I feel like there should be something. An option. Most of the Kith abilities are base-line in nature and don't really develop past that.<br /> <br /> Could always make it so that their kith ability is a 10 dot merit, and that each dot of Wyrd unlocks the next dot in the merit. Albeit, that sounds like a challenging and time-consuming proposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 01-20-2016, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T10:51:08-08:00","id":812720,"title":"","content":"Space is a precious commodity in Changeling, and kiths already take up a lot of space. It's easier to just make powers that scale to Wyrd.<br /> <br /> There might be some tinkering in this(I'm jotting notes on options we might do to see if it's feasible now that you have me thinking about), but like I said, we're at about a hundred kiths already, and there's plans on making even more. At this point, variety is the name of the Kith game, rather than deepening the Kiths.<br /> <br /> All I'll say for now if that Dave does have plans for looking at Kiths in a supplemental book-it's just not on the table yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:03:50-08:00","id":812730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/812403-options-to-expand-kith-based-abilities?p=812720#post812720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Space is a precious commodity in Changeling, and kiths already take up a lot of space. It's easier to just make powers that scale to Wyrd.<br /> <br /> There might be some tinkering in this(I'm jotting notes on options we might do to see if it's feasible now that you have me thinking about), but like I said, we're at about a hundred kiths already, and there's plans on making even more. At this point, variety is the name of the Kith game, rather than deepening the Kiths.<br /> <br /> All I'll say for now if that Dave does have plans for looking at Kiths in a supplemental book-it's just not on the table yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe it's because I'm quality over quantity at heart, but I'd rather see a handful of kiths with a good amount of depth to them rather than a vast array of options that are paper-thin. I dunno how exactly the development will go, but I definitely want to see other options presented that further flesh out the differences between each kith that's more than &quot;You get a +1 on this kind of roll and can spend energy to buff it further.&quot; Most of the options are nice, but they're all baseline effects that you start with, they don't really possess any growth of mechanics beyond having more Wyrd lets you pump your favored skill check higher.<br /> <br /> Maybe some Kiths should be consolidated? I don't know even how viable this would be, but I'd assume that over time you'll start to get Kiths that start to bump into one another mechanically and thematically so maybe it might make sense to combine certain aspects of different Kiths into a single kith?<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: One idea that comes to mind is the possibility of merging similar Kiths together, but implementing Kith-related merits that further flesh out the specific details of your Kith. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 01-20-2016, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:22:40-08:00","id":812750,"title":"","content":"Well, on that one, the market works against you-one of the big things that was heavily liked by fans in first edition was the wide variety of options when it came to Kiths. It's been shown to be profitable.<br /> <br /> I understand the quality over quantity approach, but Kiths just aren't quite the right subject base to take that approach. They've been given more punch in Second Edition, but the design has never been in favor of treating them as a tunnel to explore, more like a pocket. It's a significant nail in the persona of a character, but as it's one forced by the Fae, it's not one the invites exploration in terms of the themes of rising above what the Fae did to you.<br /> <br /> Like I said, none of that means it won't be explored-I think there's some interesting room for exploration. But between design structure of kiths, the implications of that thematically and in-character, and the popularity of variety, it's not something that can be the major directional focus of Kiths.<br /> <br /> Seemings, on the other hand....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:45:38-08:00","id":812763,"title":"","content":"I can imagine some Changelings might enjoy the idea of strengthening their kith powers to use against their Keepers or to get something more beneficial out of their hard experience. But for the most part, I think it'd be more common for Changelings to expand on their seeming, since that's how they escaped, and with relatively few seemings, it's easier to devote sufficient time and pages to that enhancement.<br /> <br /> I think it's also worthwhile to have a lot of merits that could be extensions of a kith or seeming. You're a Runnerswift? Take Fleet of Foot, Greyhound, etc to emphasize just how crazy fast you are on top of the kith blessing.<br /> <br /> One angle I'm taking with Ziggy Zapf: Gameplayer kith who went Beast by becoming a glitch 'mon to escape, and becomes a different sort of bodybuilder. Biokinesis supernatural merit represents his ability to alter his stats. (Spend willpower, transfer dots from one physical stat to another for an hour.) In-character, he's modifying his &quot;code&quot; to do it. Out of character, he's just using a merit from a different part of the ST game system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:28:07-08:00","id":812783,"title":"","content":"Well, none the less I hope there area good amount of options that can further express the otherworldly nature of a Changeling beyond just their contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:41:39-08:00","id":812797,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah-changelings will definitely be weird little alien trees. They will grow to be stranger, and the threat of becoming Stranger as a result is a staple of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:50:04-08:00","id":812807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/812403-options-to-expand-kith-based-abilities?p=812797#post812797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah-changelings will definitely be weird little alien trees. They will grow to be stranger, and the threat of becoming Stranger as a result is a staple of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope that's the case, 1e didn't seem like it had very many high Wyrd-related options. It felt very... flat? I don't know if that's the right word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:58:39-08:00","id":812819,"title":"","content":"They existed, they were just scattered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:21:10-08:00","id":812848,"title":"","content":"I have an idea. How about borrowing the Advanced and Epic Merits from Beast, and expanding them? Mortals and supernaturals could have the former, but the latter all had the Beast template as a prerequisite, IIRC. The latter's mythological feel is great for changelings with high Wyrd. I personally see no reason to limit Epic Merits to Beasts, though some might not fit thematically with certain splats. I'd house rule that Beasts, being the older brothers and sisters of monsterkind, can have Epic Merits at character generation. Other splats can have them, but first they have to reach Powerstat 6+. Let's take a look at a Merit that does something similar: Wyrdskill (Equinox Road page 15). Starting at Wyrd 6, every increase in Wyrd gives you a free Specialty in a single Skill. However, buying Specialties and Skill dots within the same category (Physical, Mental or Social) costs more XP. There could a system for Wyrd Evolution like the one in Equinox Road, which lets changelings with Wyrd 6+ gain a maxed out instance of one Epic Merit for free at each increase in Wyrd. I agree that it makes more sense to expand your Seeming abilities, since Seemings are all about choosing your own path in life. As BronzeDog said, you can expand on Kiths with normal and Advanced Merits.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'd be very, very interested in the possibility of changelings with Wyrd 10 becoming something other than True Fae. I'd also like it if turning into a True Fae was a choice, rather than an automatic downward spiral to Clarity 0. You were taken away, transformed in more ways than one to fit the whims of a monster, escaped by the skin of your teeth and started writing your own story. Would you be going back to square one if you became one of the Others, or are you only climbing higher toward something much bigger?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-20-2016, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:43:15-08:00","id":812871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/812403-options-to-expand-kith-based-abilities?p=812848#post812848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I'd be very, very interested in the possibility of changelings with Wyrd 10 becoming something other than True Fae. I'd also like it if turning into a True Fae was a choice, rather than an automatic downward spiral to Clarity 0. You were taken away, transformed in more ways than one to fit the whims of a monster, escaped by the skin of your teeth and started writing your own story. Would you be going back to square one if you became one of the Others, or are you only climbing higher toward something much bigger?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like the idea that you could avoid becoming one of the Gentry. Should be difficult though, but a possibility, rather than becoming one of the Gentry being an inevitability.<br /> <br /> Albeit, what form it would take and how it would work, I have no idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 01-20-2016, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:55:55-08:00","id":812876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/812403-options-to-expand-kith-based-abilities?p=812848#post812848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea. How about borrowing the Advanced and Epic Merits from Beast, and expanding them? Mortals and supernaturals could have the former, but the latter all had the Beast template as a prerequisite, IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>iirc, those are actually only have the prerequisite of Beast because it was a Beast book and that they'll be appearing in other gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:28:11-08:00","id":812895,"title":"","content":"A Wyrd 10 Changeling does not become a True Fae. A Wyrd 10 Changeling just has the trigger pulled back, requriring that you also drop to Clarity 0(Which does not just start automatically happening when you hit Wyrd 10) <i>and</i> make your happy ass to Arcadia, and that's if you use the Becoming Nightmare mechanic, which is and always has been optional.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not sure there's an interest in giving changelings a Archmage/Golcanda state at Wyrd 10. There's been chatter about a New Dawn-esque answer for Wyrd 0, but no &quot;I am powerful, enlightened, and liberated.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know I've lost interest in it, and this is coming from the guy who worked on the Tuatha for a while(fan work: Think True Fae for the Mortal World).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:41:09-08:00","id":812910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/812403-options-to-expand-kith-based-abilities?p=812895#post812895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Wyrd 10 Changeling does not become a True Fae. A Wyrd 10 Changeling just has the trigger pulled back, requriring that you also drop to Clarity 0(Which does not just start automatically happening when you hit Wyrd 10) <i>and</i> make your happy ass to Arcadia, and that's if you use the Becoming Nightmare mechanic, which is and always has been optional.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not sure there's an interest in giving changelings a Archmage/Golcanda state at Wyrd 10. There's been chatter about a New Dawn-esque answer for Wyrd 0, but no &quot;I am powerful, enlightened, and liberated.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know I've lost interest in it, and this is coming from the guy who worked on the Tuatha for a while(fan work: Think True Fae for the Mortal World).</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it doesn't necessarily need to be Archmage, but some interesting Wyrd 10 options. A reason for a Changeling to pursue it despite the risks.<br /> <br /> Also, what's this about Wyrd 0? This is new to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:43:19-08:00","id":812915,"title":"","content":"IT'S!<br /> <br /> A!<br /> <br /> secret.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:44:26-08:00","id":812918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/812403-options-to-expand-kith-based-abilities?p=812915#post812915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IT'S!<br /> <br /> A!<br /> <br /> secret.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, but now I <b>neeeed</b> to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:45:28-08:00","id":812921,"title":"","content":"Now I see why people did this to me not even a year ago, this is fun.<br /> <br /> But some seriousness as well, I don't know if that's going anywhere or not, so it would be improper to talk too much about it. Just, you know.<br /> <br /> Wyrd 0. It may or may not exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:56:30-08:00","id":812937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/812403-options-to-expand-kith-based-abilities?p=812921#post812921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I see why people did this to me not even a year ago, this is fun.<br /> <br /> But some seriousness as well, I don't know if that's going anywhere or not, so it would be improper to talk too much about it. Just, you know.<br /> <br /> Wyrd 0. It may or may not exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, alright. Well, I guess the question is is there a reason to pursue it? What does it cost you, and how does it benefit you? My problem always has been that it makes the game less fun because you have less options. So, how one addresses that would be (from my perspective) the largest hurdle.<br /> <br /> I know in 1e there was something about cutting yourself off from the Wyrd, I assume the idea is an expression of this in more substantiated terms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:32:03-08:00","id":812964,"title":"","content":"Wait and see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T16:03:10-08:00","id":812978,"title":"","content":"Theorizing that has a high chance of being wrong, but my first thought when I hear 0 Wyrd is that changelings would both love the idea but fear the vulnerability from the loss of power and protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T01:44:06-08:00","id":813246,"title":"","content":"I think it would be interesting for the Kith blessing to evolve not on what the kith is, but rather the changeling themselves: their personality, skills, fear and desires, and their seeming to a certain degree. A book could be done giving character examples of what a high wyrd changeling might be like, including historical examples like<br /> <br /> <b><i>Jack the Ripper</i></b> as a Razor Hand Darkling who creates surgical weapons from his flesh and blood.<br /> <br /> <b><i>King Arthur</i></b> as a Draconic Fairest.<br /> <br /> and <b><i>Edgar Allen Poe</i></b> as a Gravewrite Fairest (<i>Note: The Poe who died destitute and alcoholic was his fetch)</i>. In my head, Poe starts off as a fae-touched who gets his seeming in his quest to save his wife Eleanor (one of the few people I have researched, who Poe really cared about). He gains his kith from a True Fae that is an opponent of Eleanor's Keeper and takes the manifestation of an author. That is, he gives Poe guidance and writes Poe's story to save his wife. <br /> <br /> <i>On another note: I always thought that giving courts mantle's of six or higher could be used as vehicles to protect their clarity at a higher wyrd. As joining a court was one of the ways changelings protected themselves from the True Fae and anchored themselves to the mundane world, it made sense to me that high mantles being used to allow a player to be a high wyrd character without having to worry about clarity loss.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T16:22:54-08:00","id":813735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/812403-options-to-expand-kith-based-abilities?p=812895#post812895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's been chatter about a <b>New Dawn-esque</b> answer for Wyrd 0, but no &quot;I am powerful, enlightened, and liberated.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What is this by the way, I've never heard of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T16:29:03-08:00","id":813742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/812403-options-to-expand-kith-based-abilities?p=813735#post813735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is this by the way, I've never heard of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean's &quot;get rid of your template and all the hell that comes with it&quot; endgame resolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T16:30:15-08:00","id":813744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/812403-options-to-expand-kith-based-abilities?p=813742#post813742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Promethean's &quot;get rid of your template and all the hell that comes with it&quot; endgame resolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, explains why I never heard of it. I've never had the opportunity to play Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T18:50:39-08:00","id":813815,"title":"","content":"In 1st ed core, there's a whole section on reducing Wyrd via abstaining from magic of any kind for months equal to current Wyrd. It's implied that it's done to reduce high Wyrd to a manageble, less-terrifying level. But I could also see either a cutting-yourself-from-the-narrative method, of trying to tell no story at all (a la Dreaming!Changeling Banality), or of owning/corrupting your own story to the point where the Wyrd gives up on you (though that might be too close to Beast). Either way, heck yeah endgame options beyond True Fae or death!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","